- Native linker: some features missing, falling back to external linker

- interchange and extended float types (just aliased, no __STDC_IEC_60559_TYPES__)

- -O2 miscompile: test/test_csmith_ternary_spill.c gets the wrong checksum
  under -finline/-funroll (passes at -O1; still fails with the -O2 tail-jmp
  fast path above forced off, so it's an -finline/-funroll bug, not a tail-
  call one -- reproduces identically on a352075d, before tail calls existed
  at all). Not yet isolated to inlining vs unrolling vs their interaction;
  csmith-generated, 1450 lines, needs delta-reduction to a minimal repro.

- -O2 Tail calls — return f(args) → jmp f. Non-SSA but ABI-sensitive (frame layout, varargs callee).
  Single-scalar-arg/scalar-return case implemented (codegen.c's ND_RETURN tail-jmp fast path,
  x86-64 only); found and fixed two soundness bugs in it: (1) frame-escape aliasing -- a tail-jmp
  reuses the caller's frame before the callee's own prologue runs, unsound whenever a local
  array/struct/VLA or an explicit `&local` could still be read through by the callee (pr36339,
  pr38048-2, vect/pr44507); (2) __builtin_* names have no real linkable symbol to jmp to, only an
  inline expansion the ordinary call path provides (bswap-1). See test_opt_tail_call_safety.c.
  Still open: multiple arguments (needs the same argument-overlap care GCC's sibcall pass takes --
  see torture/20050713-1.c's own comment).

- SSA conversion for -O2, and the usual optimizations with SSA, as in xcc, antcc or ccc.

- optional solver backend for the optimizer and contracts prover with -O3
